prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a virtual microscope application that displays a 3D model of a mosquito specimen in amber. Support multiple magnification levels, a measurement tool, and light mode switching.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules inside <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/MosquitoInAmber.glb. This model is a mosquito specimen in amber;
(2) After loading, center the model in the middle of the scene and scale it to an appropriate size;
(3) Use OrbitControls to allow rotational viewing, but disable panning (enablePan = false);

[Multi-Level Zoom System]
(4) Provide 4 zoom buttons at the top of the page: "1x" (id="zoom1x"), "2x" (id="zoom2x"), "5x" (id="zoom5x"), and "10x" (id="zoom10x");
(5) Highlight the currently selected button with a different background color;
(6) After a zoom button is clicked, smoothly transition the camera to the corresponding distance using GSAP-style lerp interpolation or a requestAnimationFrame animation, with a transition duration of 0.8 seconds:
  - 1x: 5 units from the model center
  - 2x: 2.5 units from the model center
  - 5x: 1.0 unit from the model center
  - 10x: 0.5 units from the model center
(7) At high magnifications (5x and 10x), automatically increase the light intensity to make details clearly visible;

[Measurement Tool]
(8) Provide a "Measure" button on the page (id="measureBtn"). Clicking it enters measurement mode, and the button changes color to indicate that it is active;
(9) In measurement mode, when the user clicks the first point on the model surface, use Raycaster to detect the intersection with the model and display a small red sphere marker;
(10) After the second point is clicked, draw a white line segment between the two points using LineBasicMaterial, and use CSS2DRenderer or Sprite above the midpoint of the line segment to display the 3D distance between the two points, rounded to 3 decimal places; the unit may be "units";
(11) Each new measurement replaces the previous measurement result; automatically exit measurement mode;
(12) Accumulate the measurement count, incrementing it by 1 each time a two-point measurement is completed;

[Light Modes]
(13) Provide two light mode buttons: "Visible Light" (id="lightVisible") and "UV Light" (id="lightUV");
(14) Visible light mode: standard white DirectionalLight + AmbientLight, with the model using its original materials;
(15) UV light mode: change the scene background to dark purple (0x1a0033), change the lights to purple (0x7700ff), and set emissive on all model materials to light cyan-green (0x00ffaa) with an intensity of 0.4, simulating an ultraviolet fluorescence effect;

[HUD and State Exposure]
(16) The HUD in the upper-left corner displays:
  - Current zoom magnification (id="zoomLevel", displaying 1/2/5/10)
  - Measurement count (id="measureCount")
  - Light mode (id="lightMode", displaying visible / uv)

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
{
  modelLoaded: boolean,    // Whether the model has finished loading
  zoomLevel: number,       // Current zoom magnification (1/2/5/10)
  measureCount: number,    // Cumulative measurement count
  lightMode: string,       // 'visible' | 'uv'
  cameraDistance: number,  // Distance from the camera to the model center
  measureActive: boolean   // Whether measurement mode is active
}

Output a single HTML file, place it in the same directory as the assets/ folder, and run it through a local HTTP server.
